# The image never copies the workspace: the sources are mounted at run time.
# Keeping the context empty makes `docker build` start immediately instead of
# shipping 300 MB of chapters and archives to the daemon. The one exception is
# the Python requirements file, which the build has to install.
*
!tools/requirements.txt
# The engine versions are shared with the native installer, so the build
# reads the same list rather than a second copy.
!tools/craft-cli/versions.txt
